# Static-host redirect config (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify format).
#
# NOT LIVE ON THE CURRENT HOST, for the same reason as _headers: tacit.finance serves from Render, whose
# static-site product does not read this file — redirects there are set in the Render Dashboard only. Keep
# this as the canonical list to copy into that dashboard, and update it here when it changes.
#
# Why this file exists at all: nothing about these redirects is automatic on Render. Every bare path that
# works today has its own dashboard entry, which is easy to forget when adding a page. The evidence, taken
# from the live site:
#
#   /sats /weld /ceremony  301 → their directory, because each has an entry
#   /verify                301 → /verify.html, likewise
#   /tac                   200, falling through to the SPA catch-all and serving the whole dapp
#
# /tac has a directory with an index.html AND a tac.html stub beside it, and still does not redirect, which
# is what rules out both "directory index" and "clean URL" being automatic. A new page needs its line here
# and the matching entry in the dashboard, or the bare URL people type and share lands on the wrong page.

/tac      /tac/      301
/pay      /pay/      301
/pay/eth  /pay/eth/  301
/weld/keeper  /weld/keeper/  301
/pay/wei  /pay/eth/index.html  200
/pay/wei/*  /pay/eth/index.html  200

# The front page is dapp/index.html (tacit weld, formerly at /weld/); the classic app is dapp/classic.html. The
# catch-all keeps serving the front page: its head script (front-route.js) turns readable paths (/lock, /farm,
# /device/base/withdraw) into their # links on the page, and forwards the classic app's links (its tab paths such as
# /market?aid=… and /cdp, its #tab= and other fragments) to /classic.html.
#
# None of the rules below is needed for anything to work. /classic saves a page load, and /lite now goes straight to /.
# Rules sending the classic tab paths straight to /classic.html would save one more, but must keep each tab in the
# fragment (/market → /classic.html#tab=market), so they are left to front-route.js.
#
# The live /weld → /weld/ rule also matches /weld/ itself, so /weld/ must stay a file (dapp/weld/index.html, which
# forwards to / with the fragment kept) for as long as that rule is in the dashboard; without it, /weld/ redirects to
# itself.
/classic  /classic.html  301
/lite     /              301
/lite/*   /              301
/*        /index.html    200
